# What NOT to upload into an Android/iOS build.
#
# EAS falls back to .gitignore when this file is absent, and .gitignore's job is "what
# should git forget", not "what does a native build need". In a monorepo those differ a
# lot: the archive for a mobile build was carrying the docs site, the Go backend and the
# web app — roughly 8.5 MB of tracked files that no Gradle task will ever read.
# https://docs.expo.dev/build-reference/easignore/
#
# Note this REPLACES .gitignore rather than extending it, so the ignores that matter for a
# build are repeated below.

# Other workspaces — the mobile build needs packages/shared and nothing else.
/backend
/web
/site
/docs
/fly
/infra
/e2e

# Agent and tooling scratch (a full checkout per session lives under .claude/worktrees)
/.claude
/.playwright-mcp
/.github

# Standard build/dev noise
node_modules
.expo
dist
web-build
*.log
.DS_Store

# Never ship a developer's machine config: EXPO_PUBLIC_ values are inlined into the bundle
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
